---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const root=import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout title="Open-source community" description="Get involved in the HealthQualify Apache-2.0 developer-alpha community and contribute safely." active="community">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow"><span class="live-dot"></span> BUILD IN THE OPEN</div><h1>Great engineering<br/><em>is a team sport.</em></h1><p class="lead">Help improve transparent, evidence-first healthcare software tooling. Contributions must use synthetic data and respect project safety and licensing boundaries.</p><div class="cta-row"><a class="button primary" href="https://github.com/Tec-Wel/HealthQualify/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md">Contribution guide ↗</a><a class="button ghost" href="https://github.com/Tec-Wel/HealthQualify/issues">Explore issues →</a></div></div></section>
<section class="section light"><div class="container"><div class="section-intro"><span class="kicker">WAYS TO CONTRIBUTE</span><h2>Find your starting point.</h2></div><div class="pillar-grid"><article class="pillar-card"><div class="card-index">01 / HELP THE USERS</div><h3>Improve documentation</h3><p>Clarify installation, add synthetic examples and make complex qualification concepts understandable.</p><a class="text-link" href={root+'docs/CONTRIBUTOR_VISUAL_GUIDE/'}>Explore documentation contribution ↗</a></article><article class="pillar-card"><div class="card-index">02 / IMPROVE THE TOOL</div><h3>Test &amp; investigate</h3><p>Add deterministic edge cases, agent evaluation scenarios, accessibility improvements and verified fixes.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/Tec-Wel/HealthQualify/issues">Browse development issues ↗</a></article></div></div></section>
<section class="section pale"><div class="container compact"><span class="kicker">BEFORE CONTRIBUTING</span><h2>Permission, provenance, privacy.</h2><p>Read the Apache-2.0 license, DCO contributor guidance, code of conduct and security reporting policy. Never submit PHI, employer-confidential material or copyrighted standards without authorization.</p><a class="text-link" href={root+'docs/community-governance/'}>Read community policies ↗</a></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
